---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import LinkCard from '../../components/LinkCard.astro';

const relatedPages = [
  { title: 'MLB Betting Hub', href: '/mlb-betting', description: 'Complete MLB guide' },
  { title: 'Pitching Strategy', href: '/mlb/pitching-strategy', description: 'Pitcher analysis' },
  { title: 'Responsible Betting', href: '/responsible-betting', description: 'Bankroll protection' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Season-Long MLB Betting Discipline"
  description="How to approach the 162-game MLB season with discipline, managing variance, selectivity, and long-term thinking for baseball betting."
>
  <Hero
    title="Season-Long MLB Betting Discipline"
    subtitle="Managing a 162-Game Betting Season"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            MLB's 162-game season offers the most betting opportunities of any major sport—and the most chances to lose discipline. The volume creates temptation to bet every day, chase losses, or abandon strategy during slumps. Long-term thinking, strict selectivity, and bankroll management are more important in baseball than any other sport precisely because of the season length.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Why Is Season-Long Discipline Critical?" id="why">
        <h3>Daily temptation</h3>
        <p>
          With games every day for six months, the urge to bet constantly is strong. More bets means more vig paid and more opportunities for emotional decisions.
        </p>

        <h3>Extended variance</h3>
        <p>
          Even good bettors experience multi-week losing streaks in baseball. The season is long enough for variance to test any bankroll management system.
        </p>

        <h3>Market efficiency compounds</h3>
        <p>
          Over 2,400+ games, small edge erosion from poor discipline becomes significant. Every unnecessary bet dilutes returns.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Set daily limits:</strong> Decide maximum bets per day regardless of perceived opportunities.</li>
          <li><strong>Embrace selectivity:</strong> Passing on games is a feature, not a bug.</li>
          <li><strong>Don't chase:</strong> Yesterday's loss doesn't require today's bet.</li>
          <li><strong>Think in months, not days:</strong> Track results over 100+ bet samples.</li>
          <li><strong>Take breaks:</strong> Six months of daily betting causes fatigue; breaks refresh analysis.</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>162 games creates unique discipline challenges</li>
          <li>Daily betting temptation must be actively managed</li>
          <li>Variance over the long season requires patience</li>
          <li>Selectivity protects against vig accumulation</li>
          <li>Measure success over months, not days</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Related Resources" id="related">
        <div class="related-grid">
          {relatedPages.map((page) => (
            <LinkCard title={page.title} href={page.href} description={page.description} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--spacing-md); margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
